ate\": \"Find the area of a square measuring {s} {lu} on each side in {unit_label}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The unit_label slot can print sq m, so F09 produces the square meter unit. As with square_centimeter, the printed form drops the period of sq. m.\"}, \"square_unit_abbreviation\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F09\", \"template\": \"Find the area of a square measuring {s} {lu} on each side in {unit_label}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The unit_label slot prints the abbreviation sq followed by cm or m, so F09 produces the sq abbreviation.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F02\", \"F03\", \"F06\", \"F07\", \"F08\", \"F09\", \"F11\", \"F12\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"A rectangle has sides {l} {lu} and {w} {lu}. What is its area in {unit_label}?\", \"A square has a side of {s} {lu}. What is its area in {unit_label}?\", \"Calculate the area of a rectangle with dimensions {l} {lu} by {w} {lu} in {unit_label}.\", \"Calculate the area of a square with sides of {s} {lu} in {unit_label}.\", \"Find the area of a rectangle that is {l} {lu} long and {w} {lu} wide in {unit_label}.\", \"Find the area of a square measuring {s} {lu} on each side in {unit_label}.\", \"What is the area of a rectangle with length {l} {lu} and width {w} {lu} in {unit_label}?\", \"What is the area of a square with a side length of {s} {lu} in {unit_label}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"The lu slot (key length_unit, printed cm or m) and the unit_label slot (key unit, printed sq cm or sq m) are declared as separate repeats of separate generated values. Neither derived_from_values, value_derivations nor reason_kinds ties them together, and no list or bank constrains the pairing. So every question template that prints both can show side lengths in m with the unit sq cm, or in cm with sq m. Such a problem needs a length-to-area conversion that the competency does not name, and the keyed answer, which is the product of the two printed side numbers, is stated in the wrong unit. The same mismatch reaches the hint families F04 and F05, which print the unit but not the length unit, so they are not listed as failing on their own. The ranges themselves are within scope: side values 2 to 8, products printed as runs within 6 to 40, and square sides 2 to 5 with areas 4, 9, 16 and 25. Vocabulary: every term in the clauses appears in cumulative_vocab or student_vocab or introduces_vocab, and width, wide, long and unit are ordinary words not in NOT_YET_KNOWN. No NOT_YET_KNOWN term is printed.\"}",
